This is the "sum of the nth row of consecutive odd numbers" pattern. The nth row starts at `n² - n + 1` and has `n` elements, and the sum is simply `n³`.

```javascript
function sumOfNthRow(start, n) {
  // nth row starts at start + (n*(n-1)) and has n elements
  const first = start + n * (n - 1);
  let sum = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    sum += first + 2 * i;
  }
  return sum;
}
```

For the standard triangle (start = 1), this always equals `n³`:

```javascript
sumOfNthRow(1, 1); // 1
sumOfNthRow(1, 2); // 8   (3 + 5)
sumOfNthRow(1, 3); // 27  (7 + 9 + 11)
```

If you only ever need the standard triangle, you can skip the loop entirely: `return n ** 3;`.

