No — that loop never ends. `i` starts at 0 and you're subtracting, so it goes 0, -1, -2, ... and `i < 10` stays true forever. You'll spam `console.log` until you kill the process.

If you meant to count down from 10, you want the condition to match the direction:

```js
for (let i = 10; i > 0; i--) {
  console.log(i);
}
```

Or if you wanted 0–9 counting up, keep `i++`:

